<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Providence Island Company</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1630–<a href="/years/1641">1641</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Providence Island Company was an English <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joint-stock-company">joint-stock company</a> chartered in 1630 by Puritan nobles and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gentry">gentry</a>, including the Earl of Warwick, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-fiennes-1st-viscount-saye-and-sele">Lord Saye and Sele</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-pym">John Pym</a>. It founded a Puritan colony on Providence Island off the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-america">Central America</a>, which also became a base for privateering against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. The Spanish captured the island in 1641, and the company's network later formed part of the parliamentary opposition to Charles I.</p></div>
